Subject: [PATCH 9/9] server/deepseek: TF_DSV41_IMAGES=native serves video_url
 parts as timestamped frames through the image path

---
 zig/src/server/deepseek.zig | 275 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 274 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/zig/src/server/deepseek.zig b/zig/src/server/deepseek.zig
index 9f15ad51..0f9fb185 100644
--- a/zig/src/server/deepseek.zig
+++ b/zig/src/server/deepseek.zig
@@ -12,6 +12,11 @@
 //! - **Images** (TF_DSV41_IMAGES): ``placeholder`` (default) renders each image part as TF_DSV41_IMAGE_TEXT, a notice
 //!   that the model cannot see it; ``reject`` refuses such requests; ``native`` sends them to the vision tower on rank 0
 //!   (``serve.vision``: each part a sentinel, then ``<｜deepseek_image｜>``, then its span of virtual ids).
+//! - **Videos**: an image model, so a ``video_url`` part is what an image part is under ``placeholder`` / ``reject``;
+//!   under ``native`` it is frames (``vision/video.zig``): decoded by libtfvideo within main's video limits
+//!   (``videos.zig``: 2 videos, 16 MB each, 20 MB in all; https URLs unless TF_DSV41_VISION_FETCH=0), sampled evenly
+//!   at most 2 a second and TF_DSV41_VIDEO_MAX_FRAMES (8), within TF_DSV41_VISION_MAX_IMAGES (a frame counts as an
+//!   image), each frame ``<t> seconds`` then its image span.
 //! - ``response_format``'s schema joins the system block (``## Response Format``; TF_DSV41_SCHEMA_PROMPT=0: not).
 //! - Replies' reasoning as ``reasoning_content`` and ``reasoning`` (TF_DSV41_REASONING_FIELDS).
